<title>BAHRAIN: Iran joins Islamic insurance body.</title>
<headline>Iran joins Islamic insurance body.</headline>
<dateline>MANAMA 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Iran has joined the Islamic Corporation for the Insurance of Investment and Export Credit (ICIEC), an affiliate of the Jeddah-based Islamic Development Bank (IDB).</p>
<p>&quot;...The Islamic Republic of Iran has completed membership requirements in the corporation and is now eligible to benefit from its services,&quot; an ICIEC statement said on Monday.</p>
<p>The ICIEC issues insurance policies on export credits to IDB member states.</p>
<p>Algeria, Bangladesh, Egypt, Gambia, Indonesia, Jordan, Kuwait, Lebanon, Malaysia, Mali, Senegal, Saudi Arabia, Sudan, Tunisia and Iran are ICIEC members.</p>
<p>The 50-member IDB was set up in 1975 to promote trade exchanges between Islamic countries.</p>
<p>--Bahrain newsroom + 973-524424 +</p>
</text>
